WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.862
Job four: connect your team to the rest of Vanderbilt.

2
00:00:04.912 --> 00:00:11.868
Your team needs things it does not control: approvals, information, help from other offices,

3
00:00:11.918 --> 00:00:15.371
and a fair hearing when someone asks too much.

4
00:00:15.421 --> 00:00:21.463
New managers do this job least, because nobody told them it was part of the job.

5
00:00:21.513 --> 00:00:22.453
Three habits.

6
00:00:22.503 --> 00:00:30.068
Know the people your team depends on: your HCM, your Engagement Consultant, Finance, a peer manager.

7
00:00:30.118 --> 00:00:37.151
By name, before you need them. Watch for what is coming, so the team hears it from you first.

8
00:00:37.201 --> 00:00:44.537
Speak up for your team: facts, options, and a negotiated date, before you say yes to the weekend.

9
00:00:44.587 --> 00:00:52.533
For example: the week before Commencement, Events asks a grounds supervisor for his whole crew on Friday.

10
00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:56.189
He already knows the events coordinator by name.

11
00:00:56.239 --> 00:00:59.768
The schedule was on his wall calendar in March.

12
00:00:59.818 --> 00:01:06.393
At a picnic table with the printed hours, he names the conflict and offers two options.

13
00:01:06.443 --> 00:01:13.399
She picks one, nobody works the weekend, and on Commencement morning the chairs are in rows.

14
00:01:13.449 --> 00:01:17.968
This week: have coffee with one person your team depends on.

